---
source: crates/gamepadii/tests/cli.rs
expression: "help(&[\"mode\"])"
---
Switch the input mode, or with no MODE show the current one and the choices. In a gamepad mode it says which buttons to press and waits

Usage: gamepadii mode [OPTIONS] [MODE]

Arguments:
  [MODE]
          The input mode to switch to

          Possible values:
          - xinput:       XInput
          - switch:       Nintendo Switch
          - ps3:          PS3
          - keyboard:     Keyboard
          - ps4:          PS4
          - xbone:        Xbox One
          - mdmini:       Sega Genesis/MegaDrive Mini
          - neogeo:       NEOGEO mini
          - pcemini:      PC Engine/Turbografx 16 Mini
          - egret:        EGRET II mini
          - astro:        ASTROCITY Mini
          - psclassic:    Playstation Classic
          - xboxoriginal: Original Xbox
          - ps5:          PS5
          - generic:      Generic HID
          - switch_pro:   Nintendo Switch Pro
          - p5general:    P5General
          - sinput:       SInput
          - switch2_pro:  Nintendo Switch 2 Pro

Options:
      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - human:  Text for people
          - json:   The versioned JSON contract ("schema": 1)
          - waybar: One line of waybar custom-module JSON; `status` only
          
          [default: human]

      --no-wait
          Print the instructions and exit 5 instead of waiting for the button press

      --json
          Same as `--format json`

      --timeout <SECS>
          How long to wait for the button press
          
          [default: 60]

      --reboot-timeout <SECS>
          How long to wait for the pad to come back after the reboot
          
          [default: 10]

      --host <HOST>
          Talk to the web configurator at HOST (host, host:port or http://host) without looking for the pad on USB first. The default is to find it on USB and use 192.168.7.1

      --no-backup
          Don't back up the settings before writing

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
